# Implementation Plan - Rich Menu Broadcast Targeting

The goal is to allow sending broadcasts to users who currently have a specific Rich Menu assigned.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Data Synchronization**: This feature relies on the database knowing which user has which Rich Menu.
> Currently, the system does not track this in the [Customer](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx#24-28) table when linking menus.
> I will update the "Link Rich Menu" action to save this state to the database.
> **Note**: This will only track *future* changes made through this Admin Panel. Users who already have a menu assigned (or assigned outside this system) may not be reachable until they are re-linked via this panel.

## Proposed Changes

### Database Schema
#### [MODIFY] [schema.prisma](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/prisma/schema.prisma)
- Update `enum BroadcastTarget` to include `RICH_MENU`.

### Backend Actions

#### [MODIFY] [rich-menu.actions.ts](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/actions/rich-menu.actions.ts)
- Update [linkRichMenuToUser](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/actions/rich-menu.actions.ts#138-153): Add `prisma.customer.update({ data: { richMenuAliasId: richMenuId } })`.
- Update [unlinkRichMenuFromUser](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/actions/rich-menu.actions.ts#154-168): Add `prisma.customer.update({ data: { richMenuAliasId: null } })`.

#### [MODIFY] [broadcast.actions.ts](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/actions/broadcast.actions.ts)
- Update [sendBroadcast](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/actions/broadcast.actions.ts#10-62) validation to allow `targetType: "RICH_MENU"`.

### Workers

#### [MODIFY] [run.ts](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/workers/run.ts)
- Update customer query logic:
    - If `targetType === "RICH_MENU"`, fetch customers where `richMenuAliasId` (or mapped field) matches the target.

### Frontend

#### [MODIFY] [broadcast-form.tsx](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/components/broadcast/broadcast-form.tsx)
- Add "Target: Rich Menu" radio option.
- When selected, fetch and display a dropdown of available Rich Menus.
- Pass the selected Rich Menu ID to the [sendBroadcast](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/actions/broadcast.actions.ts#10-62) action.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1.  **Setup**: Go to Rich Menu page, link "Menu A" to "Test User".
2.  **Verify DB**: Check if [Customer](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx#24-28) record for "Test User" has `richMenuAliasId` set.
3.  **Broadcast**:
    -   Create a new Broadcast.
    -   Select Target "Rich Menu" -> "Menu A".
    -   Send.
4.  **Confirm**: Verify that "Test User" receives the message.
5.  **Negative Test**: Link "Menu B" to another user (or unlink), send broadcast to "Menu A", confirm they do *not* receive it.
